findings.description:
Slice plan item 5 (`300-slices.worldserver-foundation.md:27`) gives 304 these jobs:
- config for "seed, grid resolution, layer selection";
- "Pass environment context to `SimulationManager` and `engine.tick()`";
- "Handle post-tick environment writes (e.g., stigmergic trail deposits)".

The slice ships only `seed`, which it says nothing uses yet (line 149). It replaces passing the environment to `engine.tick()` with constructor injection into forces (lines 200-216). It calls `post_tick()` with no arguments and has no way to collect `trail_deposits` or `threat_mutations` from the engine. Each of these choices is reasonable on its own merits: no layers exist yet, and constructor injection keeps the `BulkForce` protocol unchanged. But the work hasn't been reassigned. No 501-507 slice is named as owner of the post-tick write-collection path, and the plan still describes `engine.tick()` receiving environment context. Either update the slice plan entry to match this design and name the slice that will collect and route the `post_tick` arguments (probably 506/505), or keep that work in 304.
